From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:50:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] Extreme Charging: implement Bodega mode controller and
 QS tile

Stock Pixel 11 series (kodiak, grizzly, cubs, yogi) introduces
Extreme Charging mode ("Bodega"), allowing relaxed charging thermal
limits and battery priority charging when fast charging under 50% SoC.

Stock SystemUIGoogle implements this via IPowerExt.setMode("BODEGA", on),
which requires hal_power_client permissions not granted to AOSP's
platform_app SystemUI.

Implement a complete, secure architecture:
1. ExtremeChargingController in system_server (com.android.server.power):
   - Acts as a power HAL client querying the Pixel Power HAL extension
     (google.hardware.power.extension.pixel.IPowerExt).
   - On boot, verifies IPowerExt.isModeSupported("BODEGA"). On devices
     supporting Bodega (Pixel 11 series), sets Settings.Global bodega_supported=1;
     on unsupported devices (e.g. Pixel 8/husky), safely disables itself.
   - Observes Settings.Global bodega_enabled to engage or disengage Bodega
     mode in the Power HAL.
   - Listens to battery updates via BatteryService, managing eligibility
     (plugged in, <= 50%, not full, not charge-limited) in Settings.Global
     bodega_eligible, and automatically turning off Bodega when unplugged
     or when battery reaches 100%.
   - Exposes state dump via 'dumpsys battery'.
2. ExtremeChargingTile in SystemUI:
   - QS tile (spec 'extremecharging') providing intuitive toggle and status.
   - Shows Active (on), Ready (eligible, off), or Unavailable (unplugged or
     battery > 50%).
   - Hidden automatically via isAvailable() on devices where bodega_supported is 0.
   - Uses stock Pixel 11 vector charging icon.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
